# Rademan — Cursor guidance

Read AGENTS.md first. It is the concise entry point for repository context and user-led development.

- The user's latest explicit instructions define the intended outcome and may override repository conventions, existing architecture, these notes and skill guidance.
- Inspect relevant source, configuration and tests before making implementation claims.
- Treat old issues, PRs, branches, decisions and AI notes as historical context, not future requirements or priorities.
- Apply current engineering best practices with judgment. Existing patterns are starting points, not immutable constraints.
- Current stack details are in composer.json and package.json; verify versions before relying on them.
- Consider server-side authorization, privacy, secure input handling and safe data access for relevant changes.
- Consider Persian RTL, responsive behavior and accessibility when relevant to the user experience.
- Run proportionate checks when useful and safe; report exactly what was and was not verified.
- Keep documentation concise and update the canonical reference when implementation or user direction changes.

See AI/DEVELOPMENT-GUIDE.md for the central engineering guide.
